{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":39.040000915527344,"text":"It looks like a small Greek temple, with columns and a pediment, but it is a tomb. It was built around 390 BC at Xanthos, a city of Lycia in what is now Turkey, for a local ruler who wanted to be buried like a Greek. Between the columns stand young women, whose clothes stream out as if a strong wind were blowing. They are Nereids, daughters of the sea, and their dresses are the closest marble has ever come to air. The Briton Charles Fellows found it in 1838 and shipped it to London piece by piece, where it was put back together as a whole façade.","words":[{"word":"It","start":0,"end":0.47999998927116394},{"word":"looks","start":0.47999998927116394,"end":0.7599999904632568},{"word":"like","start":0.7599999904632568,"end":0.9800000190734863},{"word":"a","start":0.9800000190734863,"end":1.2200000286102295},{"word":"small","start":1.2200000286102295,"end":1.6799999475479126},{"word":"Greek","start":1.6799999475479126,"end":2},{"word":"temple","start":2,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"with","start":2.7200000286102295,"end":3.1600000858306885},{"word":"columns","start":3.1600000858306885,"end":3.4000000953674316},{"word":"and","start":3.4000000953674316,"end":3.7799999713897705},{"word":"a","start":3.7799999713897705,"end":4.039999961853027},{"word":"pediment","start":4.039999961853027,"end":4.179999828338623},{"word":"but","start":4.739999771118164,"end":4.860000133514404},{"word":"it","start":4.860000133514404,"end":5.039999961853027},{"word":"is","start":5.039999961853027,"end":5.159999847412109},{"word":"a","start":5.159999847412109,"end":5.579999923706055},{"word":"tomb","start":5.579999923706055,"end":5.579999923706055},{"word":"It","start":6.199999809265137,"end":6.300000190734863},{"word":"was","start":6.300000190734863,"end":6.699999809265137},{"word":"built","start":6.699999809265137,"end":6.699999809265137},{"word":"around","start":6.699999809265137,"end":7.239999771118164},{"wor